WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
A frosty morning in the park.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.270
Two benches stand side by
side: one metal, one wood.

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.040
Rest your hand on the wood.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.100
Cool, but bearable.

5
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.750
Now rest it on the metal.

6
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.170
It bites.

7
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.830
Same park, same frosty air.

8
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.070
So why does the metal
one feel so much colder?

9
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.520
In this mission, you'll meet
the three ways energy moves:

10
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.710
conduction, convection and radiation.

11
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.850
Then you'll work out why a single
window pane lets 180 watts escape,

12
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.380
even with only a tiny temperature
difference across the glass.

13
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: explain why the metal
bench feels colder than the wooden one.
